.TH "BANDE-DIAGNOSE" "1" "" "bande-reporter" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bande\-diagnose \- make a fault report of this computer by hand
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bande\-diagnose
.RB [ \-\-send ]
.RB [ \-\-describe
.IR text ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Makes a report with this boot's and the previous boot's logs, the list of core
dumps, the processes, failed services and disk use, and anything a hang left
behind, scrubbed of personal details. It asks
the Bande report service, or makes the report itself when run as root without
the service, so it also works from a text console. Without a report server it
saves the report as a text file in the home folder.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-send
Send the report to the configured report server.
.TP
.BI \-\-describe " text"
Add a description of what happened to the report.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/bande/reports.conf
The report server, if any.
